Description: pco: vectorize UBO loads within 16 bytes before explicit IO
 Merge UBO load instructions again while they are still derefs: an extra
 nir_opt_load_store_vectorize() pass for nir_var_mem_ubo in pco_lower_nir(),
 directly before nir_lower_explicit_io. The descriptor layout is already
 known there (pvr_init_descriptors), so inline UBOs are excluded. With
 robustBufferAccess a vectorized load may span at most 128 bits: the Vulkan
 spec (shaders.adoc, Robust Buffer Access) allows out-of-bounds UBO accesses
 to be clamped as a whole only within a 16-byte window, so wider loads could
 change which components read as zero. pco_nir_opt() stays as upstream,
 including robust_modes = ubo|ssbo. With zink the descriptor set and binding
 come from deref_cast(load_vulkan_descriptor(vulkan_resource_index)).
 Replaces the earlier novec2 experiment.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
